  "notes": [
    "The load check (load-check.jsonl) loads each app in Chromium and passes when the dist/ stylesheet applied its tokens, the Expressive global exists and the console has no errors. All six pass.",
    "Two counts sit on failure paths the stand-ins never take: settings-form run 1's Retry (the stand-in rejects only with a field) and destructive-list run 2's save failure (the stand-in always resolves). Both paths are written for the real request, so they count, as the guidance-stage failed-DELETE polish did.",
    "Snackbar's root option does not move the bar into a light-DOM dialog: Utils.portalRoot returns document.body unless the root is in a shadow root. The reviewer's root: dialog fix for destructive-list run 2 would not work. This is a note for the phase 87 stage.",
    "settings-form run 1's reviewer tried one sed through Bash and was denied (permission_denials in review-result.json). settings-form run 2's reviewer says it ran one read-only sed, and its result lists no denial. Neither changed a file.",
    "filtered-dashboard run 2's page listener (index.html:247-249) does not cancel a pending filter write, the guidance-stage run 2 count. Its reviewer did not report it and the procedure adds no findings, so it is not counted. Run 1 cancels the write in its tab and page listeners.",
    "Unlabelled findings are not counted: Escape or Cancel closing the add dialog during a save (destructive-list runs 1 and 2), focus lost after a background re-render (destructive-list run 2) and a repeated field-error listener (settings-form run 1)."
  ],
